{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Symptom\n\nOn current `origin/main` (69cd2b9e15aa), this passes in the full suite but FAILS when run as\na narrow selection:\n\n    pytest tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py::test_a_marker_in_a_new_gate_scripts_head_admits_it\n    E   ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'scripts._mechanism_delta'\n\nThe failing import is inside `ratchet_head_lines()`:\n`from scripts._mechanism_delta.markers import HEAD_LINES`. It needs the repo root on\nsys.path, which in a narrow selection is not established.\n\n## Bisected\n\n    6b034b9f8224  PASS   (Make scanner-integration recipe POSIX-sh portable)\n    9c7d78127696  FAIL   <- first bad commit: 'Revert scanner-integration Verified gate'\n    cad66dd237cc  FAIL\n    457d9a20bed9  FAIL\n    a220bfafa7ae  FAIL\n    69cd2b9e15aa  FAIL   (current main)\n\nReproduced on a clean detached worktree of unmodified origin/main, so this is not a\nworktree or venv artifact. `import scripts` succeeds at BOTH refs when the repo root is\nexplicitly on sys.path, so the regression is in what puts it there during collection, not in\nthe package itself. The revert deleted scripts/install_review_scanners.py,\n.github/workflows/_scanner-integration.yml and three infra/compose files, and touched the\nMakefile; the mechanism connecting that to collection-time sys.path is the open question.\n\n## Why CI is green anyway\n\nThe default suite runs the whole tree, where something else establishes the import before\nthis module needs it, so `Verified` passes and nothing surfaces. The failure appears only\nwhen a contributor runs the module (or a small set of modules) on its own — which is exactly\nwhat an agent does when told to 'run the three gates make lint does not cover'.\n\nThat makes this a sibling of bug 1035-bed7-c855-4732, in the OPPOSITE direction: 1035 is a\nlocal green on a tree CI rejects; this is a local red on a tree CI accepts. Both erode the\nsame thing — whether a local result can be believed. A test that passes only by grace of\nanother test's import side effect is not a trustworthy oracle either way.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The narrow selection above passes on a clean checkout of main. Proven by running\n      `pytest tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py::test_a_marker_in_a_new_gate_scripts_head_admits_it`\n      (the BARE console script) and seeing it go from red to green, with\n      `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py` still green.\n- [ ] The fix makes the import explicit — the module puts the directory it imports from on\n      `sys.path` itself, derived from `__file__`, the way `scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py`\n      already does for its own `_mechanism_delta` import — rather than relying on collection\n      order. Checked: the reported `ModuleNotFoundError` no longer appears in the output of\n      `pytest tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py` run from a clean checkout.\n- [ ] A regression test pins that the reported reproduction passes when run ALONE, so the\n      isolation property is enforced rather than incidental. It spawns the BARE `pytest`\n      console script in a child from a cwd outside the repository, mirroring\n      `tests/unit/test_scripts_import_convention.py::test_repro_module_passes_standalone`.\n      Proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py -k standalone`.\n\n## Testing\n\n- **RED first:** `pytest tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py::test_a_marker_in_a_new_gate_scripts_head_admits_it`\n  must fail with `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'scripts._mechanism_delta'` BEFORE the\n  fix, and pass after. A test not seen red proves nothing when it passes.\n- **The masking invocation stays green:** `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py`.\n- **The whole module under the bare script:** `pytest tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py`.\n- **No collateral damage:** `make test` (the full suite) stays green.\n- **Gates:** `make lint` and `make typecheck` both exit 0, which includes the shrink-only\n  complexity and mechanism-delta ratchets.\n\n## Not claimed by this reporter\n\nFound while rebasing change 2619 (bug 1035). Reported, not fixed: it is unrelated to that\nchange and fixing it there would have bloated an approved change and delayed both."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788547696374066001,"uuid":"9fd43f8e-199c-4c78-aa69-6f44efefd3be"}